{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\frac{}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8665ff2cb5d95551976a92ca7e723285a252e7f14881c487db1c484961637e2"} {"question" "q-161166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$-P,\\,$ $∂P,\\,$ $∂x$"] ["text" "$-P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂x$"] ["text" "$-P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂y$"] ["text" "$P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂x$"] ["text" "$P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂y$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$-P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂y$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{z}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{z}⟩{|}_{z=x+y} \\\\  & =⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{x+y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{xy}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{{e}^{x+y}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨xy,\\,x+y,\\,{e}^{z}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(xy)\\cdot 1-(x+y)\\cdot 1+{e}^{x+y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-xy-x-y+{e}^{x+y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-xy-x-y+{e}^{x+y})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{2}-xy-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+{e}^{x+y}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{e}^{2x}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+{e}^{2x}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}-{e}^{x}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-e)-(0+\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e-1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8665ff2cb5d95551976a92ca7e723285a252e7f14881c487db1c484961637e2"} {"question" "q-161435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{4{e}^{2}+1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e-1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{8e-1}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4{e}^{2}-8e-1}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For a surface $S$ given by $x=k(y,z)$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P-\\,-R\\,)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=k(y,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨k(y,z),\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂y} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂z} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P-Q\\,\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\,\\frac{∂k}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8665ff2cb5d95551976a92ca7e723285a252e7f14881c487db1c484961637e2"} {"question" "q-161465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂x},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}"] ["math" "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}"] ["math" "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y}"] ["math" "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂x}"] ["math" "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2\\sqrt{xy}$ for $3\\le x\\le 4$ and $1\\le y\\le 2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\sqrt{xy})=\\sqrt{\\frac{y}{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\sqrt{xy})=\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩{|}_{z=2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =⟨{{\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{4xy+1}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{y}{x}}-\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}+4xy+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{[-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2x{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+8x+0-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2){[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8665ff2cb5d95551976a92ca7e723285a252e7f14881c487db1c484961637e2"} {"question" "q-161541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{4(3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7(3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7(3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2x(y+z)⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+y)=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2x(y+z)⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2xz⟩{|}_{z=2x+y} \\\\ F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2y(2x+y),\\,2x(y+2x+y)⟩{|}_{z=2x+y} \\\\  & =⟨{{3{x}^{3}y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{4xy+2{y}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{4xy+4{x}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3{x}^{3}y,\\,2yz,\\,2x(y+z)⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(3{x}^{3}y)\\cdot (2)-(4xy+2{y}^{2})\\cdot (1)+4xy+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6{x}^{3}y-2{y}^{2}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-6{x}^{3}y-2{y}^{2}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[-3{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-\\frac{2{y}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}y]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-3{x}^{3}-\\frac{2}{3}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-12-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a8665ff2cb5d95551976a92ca7e723285a252e7f14881c487db1c484961637e2"} {"question" "q-161552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "-\\frac{10}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{8}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea3d20db7333e68fcc4569ca72d4a16f2bf8c7ec6e836892bfe8e44ec34e7090"} {"question" "q-161166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$-P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂y$"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075873/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "622670271c9ef2d22f823e012fccebef71f049ef15